[10:51:33] I've redrawn the curving snake as a Solo48 model. It passes `validate_icon()` as **valid** with zero warnings, and `build_gate.py` passes with 0 errors and 0 warnings. I checked the renders at 480 px and at native 48 px in both themes.

**The drawing (VRECT_L, the suggested keyshape).** The head is a round snout at the top right with a forked tongue reaching x=40. A hollow neck, 10 units wide, runs left into a round upper loop that touches x=8. The body then turns back right as a 9-wide hollow middle run. That run narrows to a point at (31,27), where a single-stroke tail curls down the right side and sweeps back to its tip at (10,44). Nothing was copied from the trace. The generated PNG was used only to read the subject, and I found no useful Lucide snake to follow.

**Metric issues:**
- **stroke-width (info):** fixed. Everything is drawn at stroke 4 with every gap budgeted for it.
- **keyshape-short-axis (warn, 93% fill):** fixed. All four edges are hit exactly: top y=4, tail tip y=44, loop x=8, tongue x=40.
- **clearance e0/e1 (1.99):** fixed. The tongue is now a stem from the nose plus a fork 4 units further out, joined only at declared connections.
- **hole at the head (2.72 wide):** fixed. The head is the round end of the 10-wide neck.
- **hole in the body (1.17 wide):** fixed. The hollow body is 10 wide in the neck and loop and 9 wide in the middle run.

**What I couldn't keep:** a fully hollow S (both loops plus a hollow tail) doesn't fit. It needs six stacked walls, about 45 units at 9 spacing, and only 40 are available. So the lower loop and tail are one stroke that tapers out of the hollow body; the traced snake is hollow all the way to the tail. I also left out an eye, because no dot inside a 10-wide head can sit 8 units from both walls.

**Worth a look:** the hollow body ends in a sharp point where the tail leaves it. At 48 px it reads as the body tapering, but you may prefer a smoother join. I tried a shorter tongue fork and reverted it because it blurred into a blob at 48 px.

